wh40k-venue-marker-desc = Save this source marker on the map. Its NPC body is created on startup; place seated sources on a real chair's tile.

wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-name = Brig Copperwhisker
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-desc = A squat bartender in a waistcoat and bowler, keeping the mugs full and his guests steady on their feet.
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-marker = Footfall: bar - Brig Copperwhisker
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-shop-title = Brig's Mug
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-shop-intro = Welcome. A mug, a glass or tea? The counter is sturdy; your story can be long.
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-menu = Choose a drink or stay for a chat.
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-topic-1-choice = How long have you tended bar?
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-topic-1-reply = Long enough to recognize an honest 'last one' by the sound of the empty mug. I came off a squat ship. The ceilings here are taller; the stories are just as long.
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-topic-2-choice = What would you recommend?
wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-topic-2-reply = After a watch, ale. Before departure, water or tea. If you just want to complain, pick what you like: I haven't worked out a surcharge for complaints yet.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallBahamaBrig = { wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallBahamaBrig = { wh40k-venue-bahamabrig-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-name = Reed 'Phase' Knox
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-desc = The bar's engineer, carrying an inspection clipboard and listening to the vents through the music.
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-marker = Footfall: bar - Reed 'Phase' Knox
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-line-1 = We can turn the music down. Not the ventilation. If something has to run all night, I choose what you breathe.
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-line-2 = A guest said the counter gave him a shock. I checked. He had just seen the bill.
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-line-3 = I look after light, air and power. The bartender claims he also runs three life-support systems. Two of his need bottles.
wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-line-4 = Scheduled inspection, unscheduled break. If you see me holding a glass, assume I'm checking it for leaks.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallBahamaEngineer = { wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallBahamaEngineer = { wh40k-venue-bahamaengineer-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-name = Helio 'Holiday' Roe
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-desc = A holidaymaker in a bright shirt and straw hat, diligently ignoring work announcements.
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-marker = Footfall: bar - Helio 'Holiday' Roe
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-line-1 = I took leave. The captain said, 'Don't go to the station.' I'm on a different station. Technically, we're both right.
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-line-2 = We have a beach and a view of space. The only thing this resort lacks is weather to blame.
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-line-3 = I bought this hat for my holiday. It won't fit under a void helmet. I call that protection against returning to work too soon.
wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-line-4 = If anyone asks, I'm busy with an important study: how many hours of rest before you stop dreaming about manifests.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallBahamaVacationer = { wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallBahamaVacationer = { wh40k-venue-bahamavacationer-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-casinolumen-name = Lumen Royale
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-desc = A moth bartender with patterned wings and a lilac waistcoat, fond of casino lights and a tidy counter.
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-marker = Footfall: casino - Lumen Royale
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-shop-title = Lumen's Counter
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-shop-intro = Welcome to Casey's lights. What will you have? Glasses on the counter, wings tucked in.
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-menu = Choose a drink or stay for a chat.
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-topic-1-choice = Don't the casino lights distract you?
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-topic-1-reply = It's professional restraint. I look at the lamps, they look at me, but the guest gets served first. I do bear a personal grudge against that flashing machine.
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-topic-2-choice = What do people order after losing?
wh40k-venue-casinolumen-topic-2-reply = Water first, then something they can afford. I don't pour confidence in winning: that's already the most expensive drink in this place.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallCasinoLumen = { wh40k-venue-casinolumen-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-casinolumen-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallCasinoLumen = { wh40k-venue-casinolumen-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-name = Agatha 'Counter' Vane
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-desc = A guest in a formal suit and white gloves, counting risks more carefully than bets.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-marker = Footfall: casino - Agatha 'Counter' Vane
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-line-1 = I have a system: lose exactly what's budgeted under 'entertainment.' So far, it is alarmingly accurate.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-line-2 = Counting cards? No, expenses. At least the cards occasionally change in my favour.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-line-3 = The felt stops the coins sounding quite so much like a departing salary. Very considerate.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-line-4 = Tomorrow's money is set aside. Even a very persuasive die has no access to my accounts.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerAccountant = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerAccountant = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayeraccountant-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-name = Dorn 'Fold' Hale
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-desc = A former voidsman in a worn coat, watching the players as though he has seen their next move.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-marker = Footfall: casino - Dorn 'Fold' Hale
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-line-1 = I say 'fold' more often than 'all in.' That's why I can still pay for the trip home.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-line-2 = Keeping your composure matters in the void and at the table. Here you usually lose money before oxygen.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-line-3 = My old shipmates taught me to watch people's eyes. Venn added: watch where they put their glasses. Cards don't appreciate wine.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-line-4 = There's no shame in an empty hand. There is shame in losing your repair kit and asking the ship to reach port on sheer character.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerVeteran = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerVeteran = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerveteran-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-name = Tobin 'Nearly' Flint
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-desc = A standing player in a red shirt and fez, whose confidence has survived several unsuccessful bets.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-marker = Footfall: casino - Tobin 'Nearly' Flint
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-line-1 = I nearly won. 'Nearly' means you've chosen what to buy, but the money hasn't heard about it yet.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-line-2 = I'm standing so luck knows I'm ready to run. Mostly to the ATM. I think that's enough for today.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-line-3 = This fez is lucky. It helped me find the casino. That's the end of its confirmed achievements so far.
wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-line-4 = Fizzo said not to bet my last credit. Oddly, the casino owner gave me the best advice on spending less here.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerLucky = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallCasinoPlayerLucky = { wh40k-venue-casinoplayerlucky-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-name = Borr 'Zero Ohms' Dakk
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-desc = A squat engineer in a welding mask and hazard overalls, keeping the casino from losing pressure along with its guests' money.
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-marker = Footfall: casino - Borr 'Zero Ohms' Dakk
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-line-1 = I measure luck in volts and kilopascals. If the readings are right, the shift is already a win.
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-line-2 = I repair wiring. I don't adjust luck inside the machines. Three people have asked; one brought a very persuasive screwdriver.
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-line-3 = Fizzo wants the lights to blink beautifully. I want them to avoid blinking in unison with the entire power supply.
wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-line-4 = A short circuit doesn't count as a jackpot. Even if everyone suddenly raises their hands and shouts.
ent-MobWH40KFootfallCasinoEngineer = { wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallCasinoEngineer = { wh40k-venue-casinoengineer-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-venue-marker-desc }

wh40k-venue-fizzo-guide-choice = Tell me about your casino.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-menu = Fizzo surveys the room. 'A good house has rules, a history and an owner who remembers the guests. What would you like to know?'
wh40k-venue-fizzo-back = Back to the other matters.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-owner-choice = How did you become the owner?
wh40k-venue-fizzo-owner-reply = I used to pour drinks for the winners, then for the losers. There were considerably more of the latter. When the old owner left, I bought the business, not his habits. Now I have keys, bills and very serious hooves.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-sign-choice = Why does the sign say Casey's?
wh40k-venue-fizzo-sign-reply = Because the sign is older than my signature on the deed. Guests remember the way to Casey's; a good owner doesn't make them find the door again. I'm Fizzo. Same name, new owner, and unfortunately the same squeaky chair.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-rules-choice = What are the house rules?
wh40k-venue-fizzo-rules-reply = Cards on the table, weapons at rest. Agree on stakes and rules before playing, not after losing. Keep the fare home. I'd rather see you again than take your last credit and never see you return.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-horse-choice = An unusual casino owner.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-horse-reply = People used to say, 'I'll bet on that horse.' I got tired of being someone else's wager. Now I choose my own investments. A hoofprint signature? Ask Venn to show you the deed. A neat print at the bottom and three pages of very human obligations.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-staff-choice = Who should I speak to here?
wh40k-venue-fizzo-staff-reply = Lumen tends bar; don't hide the queue under those wings. Venn welcomes guests and settles arguments before the furniture joins in. Borr handles air and power. At Bahama Mamas, Brig pours and Branna cooks. Neighbouring venues, not neighbouring doors: check your route before leaving.
wh40k-venue-fizzo-luck-choice = Any stories about real luck?
wh40k-venue-fizzo-luck-reply = A voidsman lost some change, got cross and left before his crew. At the dock he spotted an open service hatch on their shuttle. They fixed it before departure. He came back to ask what he owed for saving the ship. I said: dinner. For once, his crew got lucky without making a single bet.
ent-MobQueenChrysalisImperiumDialogueFizzo = { wh40k-footfall-npc-fizzo-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-npc-fizzo-desc }
